1
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,980
=The Cruel Tribunal=
=Episode 10=

2
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,840
It's no easy feat for ordinary people
to appeal directly to the Emperor.

3
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,960
After walking through the gates of heck,

4
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,120
let alone seeking justice,

5
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,120
you might not even keep your life.

6
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:21,960
I, Legal Advocate Jiang Xiaobai,

7
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,280
have a grievance to report.

8
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:26,160
Father,

9
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,360
what is "pawning a wife"?

10
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:31,760
My good girl,

11
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,120
pawning a wife

12
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:33,760
is

13
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:35,440
not a good thing.

14
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:37,360
It is when someone

15
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,320
rents out their wife

16
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,440
to another person,

17
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:42,520
so she goes

18
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,920
to someone else's house

19
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,520
to bear children

20
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:46,760
for them

21
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,200
and take care

22
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,320
of their household.

23
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,120
This

24
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,160
is an act

25
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,800
that treats humans like animals,

26
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,160
and it's deeply hurtful

27
00:01:58,480 --> 00:01:59,280
and disrespectful.

28
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,440
Will you pawn Mother

29
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,000
to someone else?

30
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,840
Come here.

31
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,120
My good girl,

32
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,920
how could I ever?

33
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,360
When I grow up,

34
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,400
will I be pawned to someone else?

35
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:16,560
No, you won't.

36
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:18,760
Why?

37
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:24,320
Because

38
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:28,000
someone will
eventually change all of this.

39
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,520
By law,

40
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:33,280
anyone appealing directly to the Emperor

41
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,440
must cross a 30-foot bed of nails.

42
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,520
Only those who survive this gate of heck

43
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,320
prove their grievance
is true and deep enough

44
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,880
to be granted an audience.

45
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:42,280
I accept.

46
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,760
Open the city gates.

47
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,160
Open the palace gates.

48
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,560
(Even if it's the gate of heck,)

49
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,520
(I, Jiang Xiaobai,)

50
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:09,400
(will walk it to the very end.)

51
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:40,720
Kill!

52
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,080
(Sizhou,)

53
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,760
(with you by my side,)

54
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,320
(I fear nothing.)

55
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,560
His Majesty is moved by your sincerity

56
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,000
and pities your grievance.

57
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:22,600
He hereby orders the Zhaoming Office
to hold a public trial in ten days.

58
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,340
By Imperial Decree.

59
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,280
You who stand before the court,

60
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,800
what is your grievance?

61
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,840
Respected officials,

62
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:48,250
today, I am here

63
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,760
to seek justice for Qiniang
and her daughter Qiao,

64
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,440
who died with unvindicated wrongs,

65
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,750
and to speak out against the injustice
for thousands of women in this world

66
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:57,440
who are harmed by
the evil practice of wife-pawning.

67
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,040
Speak up.

68
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,160
What injustice?

69
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:01,400
Wang Wen

70
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:04,240
forced Qiniang
and Qiao to their deaths.

71
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:06,240
This is a bloody fact
right before our eyes.

72
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,120
Yet now, someone actually claims

73
00:06:08,130 --> 00:06:09,760
that there is no law
to prove him guilty.

74
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:12,680
Just because wife-pawning

75
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:13,880
has a long history

76
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,440
and is tacitly accepted by society,

77
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,240
can we allow it
to continue running rampant,

78
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,840
trampling on human nature

79
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,720
and harming women?

80
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:25,960
Advocate Jiang,

81
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,040
the system of wife-pawning

82
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,000
has been passed down
for a thousand years.

83
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,120
It cannot be as terrible

84
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,320
as you make it sound.

85
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,000
Sir,

86
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,440
out of selfish desire,

87
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,600
Wang Wen pawned Qiniang off like goods.

88
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,720
Who among you

89
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:39,880
can truly understand

90
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:40,920
Qiniang's misery

91
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,600
and Qiao's fear?

92
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:45,880
During those dark and hopeless days,

93
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,040
they endured both
physical and mental torment

94
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:49,440
until they could bear it no longer

95
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:51,060
and were forced
to resist with their lives.

96
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,240
The custom of leasing wives

97
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:54,440
strips women of what little dignity

98
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,640
and peace they have left.

99
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,960
It robs them of the true meaning

100
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,400
of being a wife and a mother,

101
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:02,040
leaving them to struggle
in agony in the dark.

102
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:03,600
Is this really

103
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,680
the kind of world we want?

104
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,480
The deaths of Qiniang and Qiao

105
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:10,040
must not be in vain
under this dark system.

106
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,160
If Wang Wen is not brought
to justice today,

107
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,040
then in the future,

108
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,240
there will only be
more victims like them,

109
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:17,600
more broken families,

110
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,680
and the hearts
of the people in this world

111
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,500
will grow even colder
and more unfeeling.

112
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,640
I implore you, sirs,

113
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,880
to uphold fairness,

114
00:07:27,090 --> 00:07:28,600
abolish the practice of pawning wives,

115
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,200
and stop this evil custom

116
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,040
from consuming more innocent lives,

117
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:33,840
so that the women of this land

118
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,640
may have the dignity they deserve.

119
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,100
Tell Official Huang to adjourn the court

120
00:07:44,110 --> 00:07:44,960
and deliver judgment another day.

121
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,160
Yes.

122
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,360
Regarding the details of this case,

123
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:04,240
this court

124
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,760
has taken note.

125
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:07,040
After I have

126
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:09,880
deliberated with the other officials,

127
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:11,280
a decision will be made.

128
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,080
Court is adjourned.

129
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:33,440
What's the matter?

130
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,500
Realize you can't do anything to me?

131
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:37,720
Let me tell you,

132
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:40,480
I'm following
the traditions of our ancestors.

133
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:43,480
Even if you appeal to
the highest authority, it won't work.

134
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:44,800
What now?

135
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:46,400
You want to hit me again?

136
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,480
This slap

137
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,040
is for Qiniang,

138
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,240
this slap is for Qiao,

139
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,400
and this slap is for myself.

140
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,160
What an interesting woman.

141
00:09:02,790 --> 00:09:03,640
Return to the palace.

142
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:05,080
Departing.

143
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,520
(You wretched woman,)

144
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,560
(just you wait.)

145
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:19,150
♪The candle burns down
to its final glow♪

146
00:09:20,110 --> 00:09:22,510
♪Cold fragrance clings to my hem♪

147
00:09:23,150 --> 00:09:24,910
♪You gently smooth my hair♪

148
00:09:24,910 --> 00:09:27,830
♪Yet your gaze drifts far away♪

149
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:32,710
♪A hidden blade lies beneath your smile♪

150
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:36,390
♪You turn away
as if nothing has changed♪

151
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:38,550
♪Step by step, I walk away♪

152
00:09:38,710 --> 00:09:42,030
♪Each step breaks my heart anew♪

153
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:47,670
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

154
00:09:48,190 --> 00:09:51,270
♪Why leave me
standing alone in the wind?♪

155
00:09:51,710 --> 00:09:54,310
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

156
00:09:54,310 --> 00:09:58,350
♪Yet all that's left
is warmth upon my fingertips♪

157
00:09:58,590 --> 00:10:01,630
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

158
00:10:02,030 --> 00:10:04,710
♪And write of every meeting
and every parting♪

159
00:10:04,710 --> 00:10:07,430
♪If next life asks
about the days gone by♪

160
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:10,670
♪I'll only say that once♪

161
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:12,910
♪I called your name♪

162
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:19,750
♪The silent stars hang low♪

163
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:23,350
♪The river keeps flowing east♪

164
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:26,510
♪I linger in the old tower♪

165
00:10:26,630 --> 00:10:30,270
♪Waiting for you,
though all is now empty♪

166
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:34,030
♪This life still owes us a bow♪

167
00:10:34,910 --> 00:10:37,710
♪May the next repay us with a dream♪

168
00:10:38,470 --> 00:10:40,710
♪Beyond here lie
endless mountains and rivers♪

169
00:10:40,710 --> 00:10:46,950
♪I dare not turn for one last look♪

170
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:50,110
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

171
00:10:50,710 --> 00:10:54,190
♪Why bury this heart beneath the frost?♪

172
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:56,830
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

173
00:10:56,830 --> 00:11:01,110
♪Now only fading warmth
remains in my palm♪

174
00:11:01,110 --> 00:11:04,030
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

175
00:11:04,470 --> 00:11:07,190
♪And paint a winter between your brows♪

176
00:11:07,190 --> 00:11:09,870
♪If we meet again in another life♪

177
00:11:10,190 --> 00:11:12,910
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

178
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:15,870
♪Was when we first met?♪

179
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:19,550
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

180
00:11:20,670 --> 00:11:22,430
♪Was when we met for the last time?♪
